  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/google-deepmind/mujoco/tarball/3.15.0",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/google-deepmind/mujoco/zipball/3.15.0",
  "body": "# Version 3.15.0 (October 5, 2026)\r\n\r\n## General\r\n\r\n1. [`1aa68e1ca`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/1aa68e1ca) [.mjz](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/programming/modeledit.html#MJZArchives) archives written on Windows now always use `/` separators.\r\n\r\n2. [`1aa68e1ca`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/1aa68e1ca) Assets in a [meshdir](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#compiler-meshdir) or [texturedir](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#compiler-texturedir) now\r\n   resolve correctly in [.mjz](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/programming/modeledit.html#MJZArchives) archives when rewritten or when the directory path is absolute, uses\r\n   `..`, or uses a URI scheme.\r\n\r\n## Engine\r\n\r\n> [!WARNING]\r\n> **Breaking API changes**\r\n>\r\n> 3. [`b3dd9e617`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/b3dd9e617) Actuator [dampratio](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-position-dampratio) now computes the reflected inertia\r\n>    $m$ at `mjModel.qpos0` as the operational-space inertia $(J M^{-1} J^T)^{-1}$ (averaged across force\r\n>    outputs for multi-output actuators such as [orientation](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#actuator-orientation)), rather than summing\r\n>    $\\text{dof\\\\_M0}_j / J_j^2$ across degrees of freedom. This accounts for tendon and actuator armature as well\r\n>    as off-diagonal inertial coupling, and avoids extreme damping values when a multi-DOF transmission has small\r\n>    Jacobian entries. In practice, actuators using `dampratio` on multi-link kinematic chains may exhibit lower\r\n>    damping than before, while actuators driving tendons or sites that span multiple joints will be damped much more\r\n>    accurately instead of being overdamped.\r\n>\r\n> 4. [`5023a4a50`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/5023a4a50) Removed the deprecated `internal` flex collision option and associated `evpair`\r\n>    structures.\r\n\r\n5. [`1b973add4`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/1b973add4) Added experimental simplified Stable Neo-Hookean elasticity for non-interpolated 3D flexes,\r\n   enabled only through `mjsFlex.elastic3d = 1`. It projects the material Hessian to positive semidefiniteness for the\r\n   solver and Rayleigh damping, and preserves the Saint Venant-Kirchhoff (StVK) default (`0`).\r\n   SNH requires the discrete integrator. The setting is not available in MJCF.\r\n\r\n6. [`2742de438`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/2742de438) The cached flex bending factor now retains cross-coordinate couplings between differently\r\n   oriented vertex bodies.\r\n\r\n7. [`eed008905`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/eed008905) Flex bending and stretching now include the motion and reaction forces of articulated vertex\r\n   attachments. The discrete integrator supports these attachments with the CG solver; fixed and independent XYZ-slide\r\n   attachments retain their optimized assembly. Elastic flexes attached to mocap bodies produce a compiler error.\r\n\r\n8. [`6224e95f6`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/6224e95f6) Added single-shot [multicontact](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/computation/index.html#coMultiCCD) for collisions with capsule geoms.\r\n\r\n9. [`ebfb4662d`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/ebfb4662d) Added the [enclosed](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-insidesite-enclosed) attribute to\r\n   [insidesite](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/XMLreference.html#sensor-insidesite) sensors, measuring how much an object juts out of a site (using directed\r\n   Hausdorff distance) and reporting signed clearance/protrusion.\r\n\r\n10. [`f80ef4244`](https://github.com/google-deepmind/mujoco/commit/f80ef4244) Fixed 64-bit model size narrowing in binary MJB serialization: [`mj_saveModel`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mj_saveModel) and\r\n    [`mj_loadModelBuffer`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/functions.html#mj_loadModelBuffer) now accept [`mjtSize`](https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/stable/APIreference/APItypes.html#mjtSize) for `buffer_sz`, supporting models larger than 2 GiB.\r\n"
}
